### Menu Chrome

Main file:

- `scripts/MenuUI.cs`

Owns the shared chrome for the full-screen menu tabs (`scenes/PlayGameScreen.cs`,
`scenes/PreGameLobby.cs`, `scenes/TrainingSetupScreen.cs`).

`MenuUI.AddBackButton(screen, font, handler)` is the only way a menu tab should
create its "leave this screen" button. It anchors the button to the screen root's
top-left corner at `CornerPad` and applies the shared red. Tabs must pass their
SCREEN ROOT, not a flow container — anchoring to the root is what keeps the
button on the same pixel regardless of how the tab lays out its own content, and
the call must come last in the tab's UI build so the button draws on top.

Deliberately does NOT cover the overlay cards (`scripts/PauseMenu.cs`,
`scripts/SettingsPanel.cs`). Those are small centred panels, so a
screen-anchored corner would place their Back/Close outside the card.

## Current Design Pillars

- First person by default
- Third person toggle on `3`
- Fast expressive movement
- Sword found in maze center before combat unlocks
- Stylized realistic retro dungeon vibe
- Modular, grid-aligned dungeon pieces
- Multi-level maze support through stair pieces

## Known Architecture Risks

- Stair pieces are more complex than flat pieces because they involve rotation, openings, height, and ramp geometry.
- Center arena stitching depends on consistent coordinate/origin math.
- Handmade maps and generated maps must use the same piece scale and connection rules.
- Collision must be generated alongside visuals, not as an afterthought.
